1:**Verdict: REVISION REQUIRED.**
2:
3:1. **H1 — High — FR-021, FR-024, BR-008: cancellation bypasses cost protection.**  
4:   **Scenario (browser/network):** A member starts processing, leaves after billable provider work begins, and 
repeats. FR-021 guarantees an unchanged counter, allowing unlimited company expenditure. Paid processing can produce 
no visible output. [OpenAI documentation](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/reasoning).  
5:   **Evidence:** [SPEC:119](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:119), [owner 
cancellation answer:91](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/state.md:91).  
6:   **Fix:** Add an **owner-approved** dispatch/attempt budget independent of successful-draft counting: cancellation 
after provider dispatch cannot replenish that budget. Changing cancellation counting instead also requires owner 
confirmation; it contradicts the recorded answer.
7:
8:2. **H2 — High — FR-024, BR-008, AC-016: quota admission and settlement are undefined.**  
9:   **Scenario (concurrency/network/crash):** At 19/20, several requests independently pass the limit check and call 
the provider. A retried POST can produce another billed request; a crash between provider success and counter update 
loses accounting. AC-016 never asserts successful increments.  
10:   **Evidence:** [SPEC:122](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:122), 
[AC-016:236](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:236).  
11:   **Fix:** Require atomic company/day reservations before dispatch, admission against successful plus reserved 
usage, request idempotency, and crash recovery. Define “successful draft” as validated generation, independent of 
saving the note. Confirm the day boundary and test competing requests, retries, reset, reprocessing, and settings 
changes.
12:
13:3. **H3 — High — FR-027, BR-001/003, §9: retained notes lack durable company and creator identity.**  
14:   **Scenario (real user):** An admin deletes a space. `room_id` is currently NOT NULL, so SET NULL fails; 
retaining a nullable row still makes existing note/item RLS deny access because both policies join through the deleted 
space. The schema also has only `edited_by`, which cannot establish the original author.  
15:   **Evidence:** 
[baseline:643](E:/projects/virtual-office/supabase/migrations/20260610183000_baseline_core_schema.sql:643), 
[RLS:256](E:/projects/virtual-office/supabase/migrations/20260610183139_enable_core_table_rls.sql:256).  
16:   **Fix:** Specify immutable, server-derived note company and creator identities using application UUIDs; nullable 
`room_id` with SET NULL; authorization/search through the retained company identity. Define company-deletion behavior 
and an owner-approved legacy-author policy—never infer creator from last editor.
17:
18:4. **H4 — High — FR-015/022, §12: provider notice can become stale before dispatch.**  
19:   **Scenario (concurrency):** A member sees “Anthropic”; an admin changes the provider to GLM; processing reads 
the latest settings and sends the transcript to GLM without the promised notice. Mid-processing key/model changes also 
have no defined behavior.  
20:   **Evidence:** [FR-015:113](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:113), 
[privacy notice:207](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:207).  
21:   **Fix:** Bind the notice/start request to a settings revision. Reject stale revisions before dispatch and show 
the new provider notice. Snapshot the provider/key/model configuration for an admitted request; prohibit silent 
fallback and require a refreshed notice for subsequent retries.
22:
23:5. **M1 — Medium — BR-003/004/005, FR-006/009/011: authorization-sensitive mutation paths are underspecified.**  
24:   **Scenario (real member):** A viewer inserts themselves into participants before authorization checks the 
resulting list. An assignee uses a broadly permitted item UPDATE to change description, assignee, or parent note. An 
existing participant grants another viewer editing rights through participant editing or restore.  
25:   **Evidence:** [business rules:134](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:134), 
[RLS requirement:204](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:204). RLS alone does not 
restrict writable columns. [Supabase 
documentation](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/postgres/column-level-security).  
26:   **Fix:** Require authorization against committed **pre-change** membership and participants, enforced at API and 
database/RPC boundaries. Completion must accept only the desired completion state. Protect ownership and parent IDs. 
Confirm who may change participant edit permissions, including through restore. Add same-company direct-database 
attacks and company-A-admin versus company-B tests.
27:
28:6. **M2 — Medium — FR-018/020, AC-010/016: persistence requirements contradict each other.**  
29:   **Scenario (provider failure):** Creating a note from a transcript saves nothing until review under AC-010. If 
generation fails, FR-020 and AC-016 require that nonexistent note and transcript to “stay saved.” Attachment failure 
likewise leaves unclear whether the old or replacement transcript survives.  
30:   **Evidence:** [AC-010:230](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:230), 
[AC-016:236](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:236), [owner F3 
answer:91](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/state.md:91).  
31:   **Fix:** Obtain an owner decision and specify separate persistence states for new-note generation, attachment 
replacement, and reprocessing. Define what exists before dispatch, after failure/cancellation, and after reviewed 
save; align both ACs.
32:
33:7. **M3 — Medium — FR-007/008/018, BR-007/011: concurrency and atomicity stop at an unclear boundary.**  
34:   **Scenario (concurrency/crash):** Transcript replacement races with reprocessing; item editing overwrites an 
assignee’s completion; restore races with editing. A crash can save summary/transcript but omit accepted items or the 
immutable version.  
