responses; AC-033 exercises delayed delivery. |
| R3-4 | Partially | FR-011 requires atomic capacity across insertion paths. AC-032’s mixed-path fixture cannot 
demonstrate that requirement: R4-2. |
| R3-5 | Resolved | FR-029 and §9 separate immutable historical UUID/name snapshots from nullable live references; 
AC-031 checks UUID preservation. |
| R3-6 | Resolved | FR-022 and AC-029 distinguish listed initial non-2xx rejections, including error bodies, from 
accepted-stream errors and unknown responses. |
| N3 | Partially | Scope, binding, midnight replay, explicit retry, and crash recovery are specified; post-retention 
replay remains incomplete. |
| N4 | Resolved | Return-time membership checks, transactional Apply authorization, and browser delivery fencing are 
explicit. |
| N7 | Resolved | Author/editor deletion preserves historical IDs, names, notes, and versions without blocking 
deletion. |
